abstract: >-
  ROMEO-HYDRA v0.2.0 elevates information folding as a base principle of
  computer topology. Any digital object induces a space; stable information
  lives in structural invariants while high-entropy scaffold can be discarded
  under a rate budget. Metaphor: the cell packs ~2 m of DNA into a nucleus
  smaller than half a millimetre by hierarchical folding that preserves
  function — the same idea applied to files, documents, ledgers and media.
  Includes romeo.topology.fold and romeo.tools.video (YC-ready offline
  compress as a media instance). Offline / Termux aarch64 compatible.
